### Task API test requests
# Run with the REST Client extension. Use the accessToken and user.id returned by
# registration, then replace the placeholders below. The team request can create
# a test team without changing the Prisma schema.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@token = paste-access-token-here
@teamId = paste-team-id-here
@assigneeId = paste-existing-user-id-here

### TASK-01: Create a team for testing and copy its response id to @teamId
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Task API test team"
}

### TASK-02: Create a task (expected 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Verify task persistence",
  "description": "Created through the tasks API",
  "teamId": "{{teamId}}"
}

### TASK-03: Verify the task is persisted and listed (expected to include the new task)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?teamId={{teamId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### TASK-04: Create a task with an existing user as assignee (expected 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Assigned task",
  "teamId": "{{teamId}}",
  "assigneeId": "{{assigneeId}}"
}

### TASK-05: Reject a request without a token (expected 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should not be created",
  "teamId": "{{teamId}}"
}

### TASK-06: Reject a missing team (expected 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Missing team",
  "teamId": "missing-team-id"
}

### TASK-07: Reject a missing assignee (expected 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Missing assignee",
  "teamId": "{{teamId}}",
  "assigneeId": "missing-user-id"
}
